From ee0b819adae152b7582e9ae7231de61344bb9196 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:00:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 086/109] dt-bindings: describe the SC7730 and SC2723 hardware
 of the gtelwifi port

Add schemas for every compatible string the gtelwifi device tree uses
and extend the existing ones it touches (sprd.yaml board and sprd,sc-id,
cpus enable-method, sprd,sc7730-dma, sprd,sc7730-mali, the PCM platform,
the Spreadtrum UART with a Bluetooth child, simple-framebuffer
backlight, smb347 extcon).

dt_binding_check is clean for all of them and dtbs_check passes for
sc7730-samsung-gtelwifi.dtb. These describe the device tree as it is;
several of them will need to change before upstream submission (the
SC2723 children belong under the existing sprd,sc2723 PMIC binding,
clock and reset controllers instead of register windows with bit
properties, a separate DSI host node with a panel).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
